{"text": "SCHWEITZER-MAUDUIT\n\n13 January 1998\n\nDr. Jerry F. Whidby\nPhilip Mortis U.S.A.\nP. O. Box 26583\nRichmond, VA 23261-6583\n\nDear Jerry,\n\n\u2018As we discussed by telephone, Schweitzer-Mauduit International is pleased to sponsor\nand organize this years TSRC in Atlanta on September 13-16\".\n\nRegistration fees for attendees are relatively low for a conference of this type. As a result,\nthe costs involved in putting on the conference, with coffee breaks and a full banquet,\n\u2018exceed revenues. As in past years, we are seeking additional sponsorship funds to offset\nthis shortfall.\n\nWe would greatly appreciate PM's help through of an event at this year\u2019s\nTSRC. Sponsorship of a coffee break will be \u20act a $3,000 level and sponsorship of either\nthe Tuesday evening banquet or cocktail hour w (000 level.\n\nSponsors will be recognized through signage at the event and in the conference program.\nMoreover, your financial support will allow us to put on a conference that reflects the high\nlevel of technical research that will be presented.\n\nIn order to finalize our budget and plans, we are trying of formalize our sponsorship list by\nmid-February. All that will be required by then will be your decision. Subsequently we will\nneed to receive a check, made payable to \u201c52 TSRC\u201d by July 1\u00ae, along with camera\nready artwork of your company logo so we can prepare the signage for the event.\n\nOn behalf of the entire organizing committee, thank you for your serious consideration of\nour request. | look forward to hearing from you very soon,\n\nSincerely,\n\nDonald A. Silberstein\n\n[AUPHARETIA, GX 20022-6248\nFAK (770) 569-4212\n\nOsoccsesoz",
